flutter_edge_ai (patch_c_api.sh section 31): FunctionGemma's tool-call
arguments in the order the tool declares them, under LLGuidance.
Upstream 9235f915 makes the LLGuidance FC grammar put a tool call's arguments
in alphabetical order (Jinja dictsort), which is what Gemma 4's template
renders. FunctionGemma's templates render them with `.items()`, the declared
order, and FunctionGemma 270M writes them in that order: forced into
alphabetical order it picked worse values (CPU greedy 18/26 vs 22/26 under
the FST provider, family defaults 43/65 vs 54/65; dropped phone_number,
swapped message/title, extra calls; macOS M5 Pro, 2026-11-25). This adds a
declared-order mode to the FC grammar and turns it on for FunctionGemma only;
Gemma 4 keeps alphabetical order.

